From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 97/97] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: the duplicate handover IRQ is noise

The CDSP firmware of the CN diting units signals the handover doorbell
repeatedly after boot; every duplicate prints an error (rate limited,
but still hundreds per boot). The handler ignores the duplicates
anyway - log them at debug level.
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 000000000..000000001 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err_ratelimited(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		dev_dbg_ratelimited(q6v5->dev, "handover signaled again (ignored)\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
